alexxx schrieb:
> 
> I had a strange experience today:
> while busy sacrificing creatures to Toth(neutral) I carelessly offered
> an ex-zombie => human corpse!
> Toth did not seem amused and
> 1) dispatched an "earth elemental of Toth". That was new to me, but
> died with a single magic missile show

I haven't done this of late, but i think converting an altar always
has a chance of ticking off the "losing" deity, which will then send a
minion.

Same-species sacrifices on a non-chaotic altar always turn the altar
chaotic, regardless of the alignment of the character committing the
deed. Excepted are (i think) the unconvertible altars - Astral Plane
and altars to Moloch in Gehennom.

> 2) the altar turned into an altar to  Anhur (chaotic). For a moment I
> believed I was turned into a follower of Anhur a prayed, but I got "You
> begin praying to Anhur.  You finish your prayer.  The voice of Thoth
> thunders: 'Thou durst scorn me?' ..." etc: new elemental, dispatched
> again.
> 
> what did I do? What will happen next?

You #prayed while standing on an altar to another god. Prayers atop an
altar always go to the deity the altar is consecrated to, once again
regardless of player's alignment. There's not much the altar's god
will do for a non-follower and your patron deity will _not_ be amused.

To actually convert your character, you need to get a sacrifice
accepted by another deity; that rarely happens by accident. Your
recent antics might put you in danger of conversion, so better find
another altar to Thoth or fight a bunch of mundane monsters before
trying to convert that altar back.

